1
00:00:01,436 --> 00:00:03,525
[bright music]

2
00:00:03,655 --> 00:00:04,917
[vegetable rustling]

3
00:00:05,048 --> 00:00:06,615
- [Hiraku] In between
winter and summer,

4
00:00:06,745 --> 00:00:09,226
the number of residents
increased again.

5
00:00:09,357 --> 00:00:10,967
After discussing,

6
00:00:11,098 --> 00:00:13,578
we decided to call this place
the Great Tree Village.

7
00:00:14,884 --> 00:00:16,973
And I ended up
becoming the mayor.

8
00:00:17,104 --> 00:00:18,975
But even though
I'm the mayor now,

9
00:00:19,106 --> 00:00:21,891
my day-to-day routine
hasn't really changed at all.

10
00:00:22,022 --> 00:00:24,154
[hammer tapping]
[bright music]

11
00:00:24,285 --> 00:00:25,634
Huh?

12
00:00:25,764 --> 00:00:28,071
- Mayor.

13
00:00:28,202 --> 00:00:30,117
There's a messenger from
the Demonic Kingdom.

14
00:00:30,247 --> 00:00:32,554
- From the Demonic Kingdom?

15
00:00:34,556 --> 00:00:37,733
["Flower Ring" by Shino Shimoji
and Aya Suzaki plays]

16
00:02:03,906 --> 00:02:07,475
[dramatic musical sting]

17
00:02:07,605 --> 00:02:09,346
- Greetings, I am Beezel.

18
00:02:09,477 --> 00:02:12,219
I'd like to meet with
the person in charge here.

19
00:02:12,349 --> 00:02:15,178
- It's my first job
as the mayor.

20
00:02:15,309 --> 00:02:16,614
That's me.

21
00:02:16,745 --> 00:02:17,659
[Beezel scoffs]

22
00:02:17,789 --> 00:02:19,269
- [Beezel] You?

23
00:02:19,400 --> 00:02:20,183
- That's right.

24
00:02:20,314 --> 00:02:21,663
I'm the mayor, Hiraku.

25
00:02:21,793 --> 00:02:25,797
- Very well, in honor
of our acquaintance,

26
00:02:29,192 --> 00:02:30,672
please accept this gift.

27
00:02:30,802 --> 00:02:31,934
[Lu gasps]

28
00:02:32,064 --> 00:02:33,718
- Thank you for your generosity.

29
00:02:33,849 --> 00:02:36,634
- I have a message to deliver
from the Demon Lord.

30
00:02:36,765 --> 00:02:39,463
He would like to discuss
the status of this settlement.

31
00:02:39,594 --> 00:02:41,204
[Hiraku gasps]

32
00:02:41,335 --> 00:02:43,598
- I don't think anyone owns
this plot of land or anything,

33
00:02:43,728 --> 00:02:46,992
but I guess it's under the
control of the Demon Lord.

34
00:02:48,559 --> 00:02:50,561
- Does he want me to pay taxes

35
00:02:50,692 --> 00:02:53,173
for all the time I've spent
living on his land?

36
00:02:53,303 --> 00:02:54,739
No.

37
00:02:54,870 --> 00:02:57,264
Maybe he's gonna tell me
to get off his property.

38
00:02:57,394 --> 00:02:59,483
Maybe it would be wise for me
to ask Lu and Tia

39
00:02:59,614 --> 00:03:02,182
for their advice
before I do anything.

40
00:03:04,967 --> 00:03:05,881
Enough.

41
00:03:06,011 --> 00:03:07,187
It's time for me to step up

42
00:03:07,317 --> 00:03:09,145
and handle my duties as mayor.

43
00:03:09,276 --> 00:03:10,886
All right.

44
00:03:11,016 --> 00:03:14,498
If the Demon Lord accepts us
living here on this land,

45
00:03:14,629 --> 00:03:18,807
then I will offer part of
our harvest for taxes.

46
00:03:18,937 --> 00:03:22,202
First, I need to show that I
have no intention of rebelling.

47
00:03:22,332 --> 00:03:23,855
As for the percentage we pay,

48
00:03:23,986 --> 00:03:25,857
I need to be strong
for this part,

49
00:03:25,988 --> 00:03:28,904
how does 10% sound?
[dramatic music]

50
00:03:29,034 --> 00:03:31,776
Crap, was that too low?
[Beezel grunts]

51
00:03:31,907 --> 00:03:33,865
- Well, then.
[Hiraku grunts]

52
00:03:33,996 --> 00:03:35,737
Are you satisfied with this?

53
00:03:35,867 --> 00:03:37,129
- Wait, what?

54
00:03:37,260 --> 00:03:38,870
I am.

55
00:03:39,001 --> 00:03:41,569
I'd like you to come pick it up
every year before winter.

56
00:03:42,613 --> 00:03:44,049
- Very well, I understand.

57
00:03:44,180 --> 00:03:46,617
That's how we will
proceed from now on.

58
00:03:46,748 --> 00:03:47,575
- [Hiraku] Huh?

59
00:03:47,705 --> 00:03:49,707
Is it settled already?

60
00:03:54,146 --> 00:03:57,062
The tax will be 10%
of our total harvest.

61
00:03:57,193 --> 00:04:00,631
However, this is limited to
what we grow in our fields.

62
00:04:00,762 --> 00:04:02,633
We won't give them any
milk, eggs, honey,

63
00:04:02,764 --> 00:04:04,374
or alcohol that we produce.

64
00:04:04,505 --> 00:04:07,072
If the Demon Lord is
interested in anything else

65
00:04:07,203 --> 00:04:09,553
then we'll enter
trade negotiations.

66
00:04:09,684 --> 00:04:11,251
[Beezel and Hiraku sigh]

67
00:04:11,381 --> 00:04:13,862
I did feel like I was too
aggressive with my negotiations.

68
00:04:13,992 --> 00:04:15,472
- I bid you all farewell.

69
00:04:15,603 --> 00:04:17,779
- So I sent him home
with a present.

70
00:04:20,434 --> 00:04:22,827
I hope I handled that
the right way.

71
00:04:22,958 --> 00:04:25,526
- I think you did
a pretty good job.

72
00:04:25,656 --> 00:04:27,354
Since we're paying them taxes,

73
00:04:27,484 --> 00:04:29,660
we're technically under
the Demon Lords protection

74
00:04:29,791 --> 00:04:30,748
from now on.

75
00:04:30,879 --> 00:04:32,359
- Yes, indeed.

76
00:04:32,489 --> 00:04:36,058
But even still,
[giggles] only 10%?

77
00:04:36,188 --> 00:04:40,105
Usually the going rate is
supposed to be 50 or 60%.

78
00:04:40,236 --> 00:04:41,455
- What?

79
00:04:41,585 --> 00:04:42,804
- Having them come to
collect the payment

80
00:04:42,934 --> 00:04:44,327
was a good decision.

81
00:04:44,458 --> 00:04:46,373
It forces them to
officially recognize

82
00:04:46,503 --> 00:04:48,157
our residents
in the forest.

83
00:04:48,288 --> 00:04:50,768
- And if they're only coming
to collect once a year,

84
00:04:50,899 --> 00:04:53,597
they won't be able to measure
everything we produce.

85
00:04:53,728 --> 00:04:56,383
In other words, we just bought
the protection of the Demon Lord

86
00:04:56,513 --> 00:04:58,907
for a real tax rate
of under 10%.

87
00:04:59,037 --> 00:05:00,648
- Well done, Mayor Hiraku.

88
00:05:00,778 --> 00:05:02,214
- Really?

89
00:05:02,345 --> 00:05:04,478
- And to top it off,
they brought this present,

90
00:05:04,608 --> 00:05:08,090
medicine that works if you drink
it or apply it to an injury.

91
00:05:08,220 --> 00:05:09,918
- Wow.

92
00:05:10,048 --> 00:05:11,398
- [Grattz] What?

93
00:05:11,528 --> 00:05:13,748
They're submitting to
our military force?

94
00:05:13,878 --> 00:05:15,576
- [Beezel] Yes.

95
00:05:15,706 --> 00:05:18,883
- [Grattz] Even though they have
the strength to defeat wyvern?

96
00:05:19,014 --> 00:05:20,929
- Surely they're
up to something.

97
00:05:21,059 --> 00:05:22,800
- I had the same suspicion.

98
00:05:22,931 --> 00:05:25,020
I had no choice but to
accept their offer.

99
00:05:25,150 --> 00:05:26,587
- [Randan] But why?

100
00:05:26,717 --> 00:05:29,154
- The Vampire Princess
and Angel of Annihilation.

101
00:05:29,285 --> 00:05:30,895
- [Grattz] What?

102
00:05:31,026 --> 00:05:35,335
The great sage, Lulucy, and
the strongest of all the angels?

103
00:05:35,465 --> 00:05:36,510
- No way! [shivers]

104
00:05:36,640 --> 00:05:38,425
- [Beezel] And that's not all.

105
00:05:38,555 --> 00:05:39,948
There was an army of high elves

106
00:05:40,078 --> 00:05:42,124
and a pack of inferno wolves.

107
00:05:42,254 --> 00:05:43,647
- [Grattz] You're joking.

108
00:05:43,778 --> 00:05:46,650
- And the group that
guided me to their leader

109
00:05:46,781 --> 00:05:48,870
was the trio of Killer Angels.

110
00:05:49,000 --> 00:05:50,306
I thought my life was over.

111
00:05:50,437 --> 00:05:52,874
- [Grattz] [groans]
If that's it,

112
00:05:53,004 --> 00:05:55,833
then I see how they were
able to take down wyvern.

113
00:05:55,964 --> 00:05:58,575
- Then he suggested that
they be under the protection

114
00:05:58,706 --> 00:06:00,490
of the Demon Lord's army.

115
00:06:00,621 --> 00:06:01,970
I could not refuse.

116
00:06:02,100 --> 00:06:04,102
If I had, they would've
immediately gathered

117
00:06:04,233 --> 00:06:05,974
to become an enemy force.

118
00:06:06,104 --> 00:06:07,367
- No way.

119
00:06:07,497 --> 00:06:08,803
- [Beezel] Silver lining
in all of this

120
00:06:08,933 --> 00:06:11,196
is that we were able to
negotiate amicably.

121
00:06:11,327 --> 00:06:13,198
They even gave me a gift.

122
00:06:13,329 --> 00:06:14,504
- Oh?

123
00:06:14,635 --> 00:06:15,679
What do you think it is?

124
00:06:15,810 --> 00:06:17,594
- I haven't looked yet.
- Open it.

125
00:06:17,725 --> 00:06:18,900
- [Beezel] We need to
consult the Demon Lord.

126
00:06:19,030 --> 00:06:20,423
- [Randan] It's over,
we're finished.

127
00:06:20,554 --> 00:06:21,642
- [Grattz] And what if
it's something dangerous?

128
00:06:21,772 --> 00:06:22,512
[wrapping paper tearing]
- Hey, wait!

129
00:06:22,643 --> 00:06:24,035
- Hmm, fruit?

130
00:06:24,993 --> 00:06:26,429
They look like appos,

131
00:06:26,560 --> 00:06:28,953
but the shape and color
are much nicer.

132
00:06:29,084 --> 00:06:31,652
Better check if they're
poisoned. [munches]

133
00:06:31,782 --> 00:06:32,783
- Hey!

134
00:06:32,914 --> 00:06:34,872
- Whoa, this is really good.

135
00:06:35,003 --> 00:06:36,178
It's great.

136
00:06:36,308 --> 00:06:37,092
- You can't just go
and eat those.

137
00:06:37,222 --> 00:06:38,485
[bright music]
Oh.

138
00:06:39,529 --> 00:06:41,313
This cloth.

139
00:06:41,444 --> 00:06:42,619
It can't.

140
00:06:42,750 --> 00:06:44,447
Is this from a demon spider?

141
00:06:44,578 --> 00:06:46,710
No, a great demon spider.

142
00:06:46,841 --> 00:06:47,929
- You're joking.

143
00:06:48,059 --> 00:06:49,365
Didn't one of those fight one

144
00:06:49,496 --> 00:06:51,889
of the previous Demon Lords
to a standstill?

145
00:06:52,020 --> 00:06:53,804
They have one of those too?

146
00:06:53,935 --> 00:06:55,589
- I'm resigning.
- Randan!

147
00:06:55,719 --> 00:06:58,069
Randan!

148
00:06:58,200 --> 00:07:00,289
[leaves rustling]

149
00:07:00,420 --> 00:07:02,422
- Uh.

150
00:07:02,552 --> 00:07:04,641
[dramatic music]

151
00:07:04,772 --> 00:07:06,556
- My name is Dryme.

152
00:07:06,687 --> 00:07:09,516
I am the one true
ruler of the Dragons.

153
00:07:09,646 --> 00:07:13,868
[light upbeat music]

154
00:07:13,998 --> 00:07:15,957
- This is a present
from Lord Dryme.

155
00:07:16,087 --> 00:07:17,959
We hope you will accept it.

156
00:07:18,089 --> 00:07:19,395
- Sure.

157
00:07:19,526 --> 00:07:22,267
Wow, it looks really expensive,

158
00:07:22,398 --> 00:07:24,966
but it seems like kind of
a violent gift.

159
00:07:25,096 --> 00:07:26,968
Thank you for
the wonderful gift.

160
00:07:27,098 --> 00:07:28,186
It's lovely.

161
00:07:28,317 --> 00:07:29,492
- [Gucci] It's our pleasure.

162
00:07:29,623 --> 00:07:31,146
- So what's the purpose of your
visit

163
00:07:31,276 --> 00:07:32,756
to the Great Tree Village today?

164
00:07:32,887 --> 00:07:33,801
- Right.

165
00:07:33,931 --> 00:07:35,629
My good master, Lord Dryme,

166
00:07:35,759 --> 00:07:38,283
has his lair located
just to the south of here.

167
00:07:39,763 --> 00:07:41,809
There's quite a bit of
distance between us,

168
00:07:41,939 --> 00:07:44,115
however we consider
you our neighbors.

169
00:07:44,246 --> 00:07:46,204
We've come here to offer
a formal greeting.

170
00:07:46,335 --> 00:07:48,424
- That's very polite
of you, sir.

171
00:07:48,555 --> 00:07:51,122
By the way, is there any
particular reason

172
00:07:51,253 --> 00:07:52,820
that your master is
bowing his head?

173
00:07:52,950 --> 00:07:55,692
- My deepest apologies
for that, good sir.

174
00:07:55,823 --> 00:07:58,303
Master, would you kindly
please raise your head?

175
00:07:58,434 --> 00:07:59,957
- What? Sure.

176
00:08:00,088 --> 00:08:01,655
- Since you came
all the way here

177
00:08:01,785 --> 00:08:03,570
I'd like to invite you inside,

178
00:08:03,700 --> 00:08:06,181
but that seems hard
given your size.

179
00:08:06,311 --> 00:08:08,357
- You're absolutely right.

180
00:08:08,488 --> 00:08:11,447
Master, please change
into your smaller form.

181
00:08:11,578 --> 00:08:13,841
[Dryme grunts]

182
00:08:13,971 --> 00:08:16,670
[smoke whooshes]
[light cheery music]

183
00:08:16,800 --> 00:08:19,499
Now, introduce yourself again.

184
00:08:21,762 --> 00:08:23,633
- My name is Dryme.

185
00:08:23,764 --> 00:08:26,244
I am the one true
ruler of the Dragons.

186
00:08:26,375 --> 00:08:29,683
- [Hiraku] Okay, I wonder
if he memorized that line

187
00:08:29,813 --> 00:08:31,685
so he wouldn't mess up
his introduction.

188
00:08:31,815 --> 00:08:34,688
- Man, this place is great.

189
00:08:34,818 --> 00:08:36,516
This booze is great.

190
00:08:36,646 --> 00:08:37,647
I'm never going home.

191
00:08:37,778 --> 00:08:39,127
I'm gonna live right here.

192
00:08:39,257 --> 00:08:40,868
- You can't do that.

193
00:08:40,998 --> 00:08:42,304
There will be a lot of people
who will get very upset

194
00:08:42,434 --> 00:08:43,523
if you don't protect your home.

195
00:08:43,653 --> 00:08:44,785
- I'll be fine here.

196
00:08:44,915 --> 00:08:46,874
I can intercept any attackers.

197
00:08:47,004 --> 00:08:48,658
- I know that, master.

198
00:08:48,789 --> 00:08:51,095
However, it would be a
nuisance for everyone here

199
00:08:51,226 --> 00:08:53,010
if you were to stay too long.

200
00:08:53,141 --> 00:08:54,185
[Dryme groans]

201
00:08:54,316 --> 00:08:55,970
Now let's be on our way

202
00:08:56,100 --> 00:08:58,799
while they're still happy
to call us their guests.

203
00:08:58,929 --> 00:09:01,323
They were even kind enough
to gift to us.

204
00:09:01,453 --> 00:09:02,585
- [Dryme] Oh yeah.

205
00:09:02,716 --> 00:09:04,674
They give us those
appo-looking things.

206
00:09:04,805 --> 00:09:06,284
- They're called apples

207
00:09:06,415 --> 00:09:08,548
and don't worry they
gave us plenty of them.

208
00:09:08,678 --> 00:09:10,854
- [Dryme] Yeah, yeah, whatever.

209
00:09:10,985 --> 00:09:12,682
I'm heading home.

210
00:09:12,813 --> 00:09:15,467
- Don't transform yet
until you're outside, okay?

211
00:09:16,817 --> 00:09:18,079
- [Dryme] Wee, I'm flying!
[wings whooshing]

212
00:09:18,209 --> 00:09:19,950
- I know I should have
thought of this sooner

213
00:09:20,081 --> 00:09:21,996
but I should really decide
how the Great Tree Village

214
00:09:22,126 --> 00:09:25,913
is going to handle visitors,
welcome guests or otherwise,

215
00:09:26,043 --> 00:09:27,784
diplomatic relations.

216
00:09:27,915 --> 00:09:31,092
Ugh, this is all getting
complicated really fast.

217
00:09:32,572 --> 00:09:35,357
I've been thinking about
a lot of things since then,

218
00:09:35,487 --> 00:09:39,317
and I believe it's not good
for us to keep visitors outside

219
00:09:39,448 --> 00:09:41,015
when greeting them.

220
00:09:41,145 --> 00:09:44,627
With that said, I'm not
comfortable inviting them in.

221
00:09:44,758 --> 00:09:46,411
So I've decided that
we should build

222
00:09:46,542 --> 00:09:48,152
a guest house for visitors.

223
00:09:48,283 --> 00:09:50,981
I was thinking a house
able to fit four people

224
00:09:51,112 --> 00:09:52,461
would be enough.

225
00:09:52,592 --> 00:09:54,898
- [Lea] No, I think that
would be far too small.

226
00:09:55,029 --> 00:09:57,466
- Right, anyone coming
to this village

227
00:09:57,597 --> 00:09:58,728
needs to climb mountains

228
00:09:58,859 --> 00:10:00,425
and make it safely
through the forest.

229
00:10:00,556 --> 00:10:02,950
Our visitors up until now
have been servants

230
00:10:03,080 --> 00:10:04,342
of the Demon Lord or dragons.

231
00:10:04,473 --> 00:10:06,388
However, normally when
people come here

232
00:10:06,518 --> 00:10:08,564
they'll be doing it
in large groups.

233
00:10:08,695 --> 00:10:11,959
- If that's the case, then I
think we should play it safe

234
00:10:12,089 --> 00:10:14,918
and build a house that can
fit 30 people comfortably.

235
00:10:15,049 --> 00:10:16,485
- 30?

236
00:10:16,616 --> 00:10:18,226
- [Lea] We'll make the
first floor an open space

237
00:10:18,356 --> 00:10:19,706
designed to hold feasts.

238
00:10:19,836 --> 00:10:21,446
- And we can make the
second floor into bedrooms

239
00:10:21,577 --> 00:10:23,840
for our guests if they
wanna stay a bit longer.

240
00:10:23,971 --> 00:10:25,625
- Hmm, that works.
[bright cheery music]

241
00:10:25,755 --> 00:10:28,366
And that's how we got started
building a guest house

242
00:10:28,497 --> 00:10:30,630
for any potential visitors.

243
00:10:30,760 --> 00:10:33,850
Next, I wanted to work on
how we greet new guests.

244
00:10:33,981 --> 00:10:35,330
Granmaria and the angels

245
00:10:35,460 --> 00:10:37,288
are in charge of
defending the perimeter.

246
00:10:37,419 --> 00:10:39,073
[swords flicking]

247
00:10:39,203 --> 00:10:41,858
And rather than finding visitors
and guiding them here,

248
00:10:41,989 --> 00:10:43,338
they would capture visitors

249
00:10:43,468 --> 00:10:45,645
and bring them to
the village entrance.

250
00:10:45,775 --> 00:10:48,952
On top of that, when Zabuton
sounded the warning alarm,

251
00:10:49,083 --> 00:10:50,824
everyone would
grab their weapons

252
00:10:50,954 --> 00:10:53,914
and get ready for battle.

253
00:10:54,044 --> 00:10:57,700
It's a long way off
from a proper welcome.

254
00:10:57,831 --> 00:11:00,442
So we came up with a
new signal for visitors.

255
00:11:01,182 --> 00:11:03,184
[bell ringing]

256
00:11:03,314 --> 00:11:06,578
Lea and the elves made a bell.

257
00:11:06,709 --> 00:11:09,190
Next, we discussed how
we treated our guests.

258
00:11:09,320 --> 00:11:12,062
I suggested that Lu, Tia,
and I would be the ones

259
00:11:12,193 --> 00:11:13,847
to greet the guests.

260
00:11:13,977 --> 00:11:16,414
- I cannot agree with using
such a small welcoming party.

261
00:11:16,545 --> 00:11:17,720
- She's right on that.

262
00:11:17,851 --> 00:11:19,330
Enemies might take advantage

263
00:11:19,461 --> 00:11:21,724
and sneak in
disguised as visitors.

264
00:11:21,855 --> 00:11:24,640
- [sighs] My idea was rejected,

265
00:11:24,771 --> 00:11:29,558
so we added a few high elves,
a scattering of ogre maids,

266
00:11:29,689 --> 00:11:32,343
and lizardmen to
our welcoming party.

267
00:11:32,474 --> 00:11:35,738
Flora wanted to be part of
our welcoming party as well,

268
00:11:35,869 --> 00:11:37,740
but I asked her to keep
an eye on any visitors

269
00:11:37,871 --> 00:11:39,611
that stay here until night fall.

270
00:11:39,742 --> 00:11:40,569
- Understood.

271
00:11:40,700 --> 00:11:42,179
Please leave it to me.

272
00:11:42,310 --> 00:11:43,703
If you'd like,

273
00:11:43,833 --> 00:11:46,227
I can keep watch the
entire time they're here.

274
00:11:46,357 --> 00:11:48,185
- That's when I learned
that Flora and Lu

275
00:11:48,316 --> 00:11:51,145
could go several days
without sleeping and be fine,

276
00:11:51,275 --> 00:11:54,148
but I still told them
not to overdo it.

277
00:11:54,278 --> 00:11:56,019
[bell ringing]

278
00:11:56,150 --> 00:11:59,588
All the preparation
we did got put to use,

279
00:11:59,719 --> 00:12:01,938
much sooner than I expected.

280
00:12:02,765 --> 00:12:04,245
- My name is Garf.

281
00:12:04,375 --> 00:12:06,290
We have traveled from
a place in the mountains

282
00:12:06,421 --> 00:12:08,771
east of here called
Howling Village.

283
00:12:08,902 --> 00:12:11,774
We want to establish
relations with your village.

284
00:12:12,557 --> 00:12:14,472
- Let me handle this.

285
00:12:14,603 --> 00:12:16,997
That must have been
a tough journey.

286
00:12:17,127 --> 00:12:19,260
The Great Tree Village
welcomes you.

287
00:12:19,390 --> 00:12:20,740
- We thank you.

288
00:12:20,870 --> 00:12:22,654
- I would like to take you
to our guest house

289
00:12:22,785 --> 00:12:24,047
so that you can rest.

290
00:12:24,178 --> 00:12:26,615
Are these all of the
travelers in your group?

291
00:12:26,746 --> 00:12:28,225
- Yes, they are.

292
00:12:28,356 --> 00:12:29,661
- [Lu] I see.

293
00:12:29,792 --> 00:12:32,403
Then we'll treat
the others as enemies.

294
00:12:32,534 --> 00:12:34,928
- [Hiraku] What's she
talking about?

295
00:12:35,058 --> 00:12:38,453
[canines growling]

296
00:12:39,889 --> 00:12:42,022
- [Garf] Hmm, sorry about that.

297
00:12:42,152 --> 00:12:44,067
It looks like we had
a few stragglers.

298
00:12:44,198 --> 00:12:45,808
- Well, that was dangerous.

299
00:12:45,939 --> 00:12:47,592
You should really make sure
everyone is together

300
00:12:47,723 --> 00:12:49,551
before you enter the village.

301
00:12:49,681 --> 00:12:51,422
And it would be wise of you
to behave yourselves

302
00:12:51,553 --> 00:12:53,120
while you're here.

303
00:12:53,250 --> 00:12:55,339
There are people that even I
need to watch myself around.

304
00:12:56,253 --> 00:12:57,428
- I understand.

305
00:12:57,559 --> 00:12:58,908
You have my word.

306
00:12:59,039 --> 00:13:01,606
- Then follow me
to our guest house.

307
00:13:03,783 --> 00:13:05,349
- Welcome to our village.

308
00:13:05,480 --> 00:13:07,308
- [All] Welcome to our village.

309
00:13:07,438 --> 00:13:09,571
[beastmen gasping]

310
00:13:09,701 --> 00:13:12,052
- [[Hiraku] Great, we've
taken our first step

311
00:13:12,182 --> 00:13:13,967
towards real hospitality.

312
00:13:14,097 --> 00:13:16,796
- Stay here and enjoy
yourselves please.

313
00:13:16,926 --> 00:13:19,276
[beastmen chattering]

314
00:13:19,973 --> 00:13:21,017
[lock thuds]

315
00:13:21,148 --> 00:13:22,410
- What are you doing?

316
00:13:22,540 --> 00:13:24,064
It seems more like you're
trapping enemies

317
00:13:24,194 --> 00:13:25,587
than welcoming guests.

318
00:13:25,717 --> 00:13:28,285
- [Tia] Mayor,
haven't you noticed.

319
00:13:28,416 --> 00:13:29,721
- [Hiraku] Huh?

320
00:13:29,852 --> 00:13:31,854
- When visitors come to
establish relations,

321
00:13:31,985 --> 00:13:34,117
they always bring some
sort of offering with them.

322
00:13:34,248 --> 00:13:38,252
Even that dragon
brought something.

323
00:13:38,382 --> 00:13:39,993
- You think they
aren't friendly?

324
00:13:40,123 --> 00:13:42,212
- I can't say for sure exactly.

325
00:13:42,343 --> 00:13:44,345
If they don't follow
the normal rules,

326
00:13:44,475 --> 00:13:47,217
then they don't get the
normal visitor treatment.

327
00:13:47,348 --> 00:13:48,436
- I see.

328
00:13:48,566 --> 00:13:49,872
- I'm concerned about
them leaving

329
00:13:50,003 --> 00:13:51,569
two troops hiding
in the woods.

330
00:13:51,700 --> 00:13:54,181
That's why we knocked
our hospitality level

331
00:13:54,311 --> 00:13:56,052
down a notch or two for them.

332
00:13:56,183 --> 00:13:58,315
- Didn't Kudel or the other
girls spot those troops

333
00:13:58,446 --> 00:14:00,361
while making their way
through the forest?

334
00:14:00,491 --> 00:14:02,145
- They noticed them

335
00:14:02,276 --> 00:14:04,495
but decided those troops weren't
a threat and ignored them.

336
00:14:04,626 --> 00:14:06,323
I planned to
punish them all later.

337
00:14:06,454 --> 00:14:07,847
- Go easy on them.

338
00:14:07,977 --> 00:14:10,153
- I'll let them off
with a warning.

339
00:14:12,286 --> 00:14:15,202
[food sizzling]
[Hiraku groans]

340
00:14:16,899 --> 00:14:18,379
- [Anne] Is something
the matter?

341
00:14:18,509 --> 00:14:20,033
- Oh, it's nothing.

342
00:14:20,163 --> 00:14:21,643
It's just that the food
you made for Dryme-

343
00:14:21,773 --> 00:14:24,820
- Do you think this
isn't up to par?

344
00:14:24,951 --> 00:14:26,561
- Well, something like that.

345
00:14:26,691 --> 00:14:29,651
- I'm sure that you've
realized by now,

346
00:14:29,781 --> 00:14:32,872
but this is the treatment
for guests who bring nothing.

347
00:14:33,002 --> 00:14:34,264
- I see.

348
00:14:36,353 --> 00:14:38,138
Oh, so does that mean

349
00:14:38,268 --> 00:14:40,618
you don't plan on
offering them any wine?

350
00:14:40,749 --> 00:14:42,707
[Anne groans]
I see.

351
00:14:42,838 --> 00:14:45,014
[beastmen chattering]

352
00:14:45,145 --> 00:14:48,496
I feel terrible offering
them such a meager meal.

353
00:14:48,626 --> 00:14:51,281
- Please erase yourself
of such emotions.

354
00:14:51,412 --> 00:14:52,630
- She's right.

355
00:14:52,761 --> 00:14:55,111
They're here for
important negotiations.

356
00:14:55,242 --> 00:14:57,897
Our goal is to find out
exactly what they're after.

357
00:14:58,027 --> 00:15:00,203
- Everyone besides you
was completely against

358
00:15:00,334 --> 00:15:01,465
offering them any wine.

359
00:15:01,596 --> 00:15:03,032
You forced us to
give it to them.

360
00:15:03,163 --> 00:15:04,468
- [Beastmen] Cheers.

361
00:15:04,599 --> 00:15:06,383
- And I'm glad that
you all let me do it.

362
00:15:06,514 --> 00:15:09,343
That said, it's just
two cups per person.

363
00:15:09,473 --> 00:15:10,822
[beastman retches]

364
00:15:10,953 --> 00:15:13,216
Those were the restrictions
put in place.

365
00:15:13,347 --> 00:15:15,566
The fact remains,
they came all the way here.

366
00:15:15,697 --> 00:15:17,655
Until we determined
they're enemies,

367
00:15:17,786 --> 00:15:19,440
I wanna show them kindness.

368
00:15:19,570 --> 00:15:22,443
First, I wanna find out
why they're here.

369
00:15:22,573 --> 00:15:26,186
Uh, I'm sure I'm revealing my
own ignorance in asking this,

370
00:15:26,316 --> 00:15:28,928
but just what kind of place
is Howling Village?

371
00:15:29,058 --> 00:15:30,668
- Well, some say
it's been around

372
00:15:30,799 --> 00:15:32,192
for over a thousand years,

373
00:15:32,322 --> 00:15:33,845
but in reality,

374
00:15:33,976 --> 00:15:36,152
I think it's really only been
about 500 years or so.

375
00:15:36,283 --> 00:15:39,547
Man, those older guys sure take
pride in the weirdest stuff.

376
00:15:39,677 --> 00:15:41,897
- You got that right.
[beastmen laugh]

377
00:15:42,028 --> 00:15:43,768
- What we call Howling Village
is a place

378
00:15:43,899 --> 00:15:47,163
of five small settlements of
about a hundred people or so

379
00:15:47,294 --> 00:15:49,383
and most of the population
are beastmen.

380
00:15:49,513 --> 00:15:51,472
- You got that right. [laughs]

381
00:15:51,602 --> 00:15:53,735
- Howling Village is
made up of people

382
00:15:53,865 --> 00:15:56,085
who make their living
hunting or mining.

383
00:15:56,216 --> 00:15:59,132
Up until now, they've managed
to survive by trading

384
00:15:59,262 --> 00:16:01,699
with a human village
across the mountains.

385
00:16:01,830 --> 00:16:03,745
But lately there's been
some trouble there

386
00:16:03,875 --> 00:16:06,748
and the trade between them
has become unstable.

387
00:16:06,878 --> 00:16:09,403
That's why they're looking for
someone new to trade with

388
00:16:09,533 --> 00:16:12,101
and they settled on
our Great Tree Village.

389
00:16:12,232 --> 00:16:14,016
So where did you learn
about our village?

390
00:16:14,147 --> 00:16:16,758
- We got word from one of
the Demon Lord's people.

391
00:16:16,888 --> 00:16:18,325
- Huh?

392
00:16:18,455 --> 00:16:20,805
- Man, if we stayed outside
hiding the whole time

393
00:16:20,936 --> 00:16:22,938
we would've missed
this great meal.

394
00:16:23,069 --> 00:16:24,722
I'm so glad we didn't.

395
00:16:24,853 --> 00:16:27,029
- Why were you hiding
in the first place?

396
00:16:27,160 --> 00:16:29,466
- You need to be on guard
for the first visit.

397
00:16:29,597 --> 00:16:31,294
Plus, if something were
to happen there

398
00:16:31,425 --> 00:16:33,775
someone needs to go back and
tell the rest of the village.

399
00:16:33,905 --> 00:16:35,646
- [Tia] Oh?

400
00:16:35,777 --> 00:16:38,910
- [Hiraku] She's doing a good
job of gathering information.

401
00:16:39,041 --> 00:16:40,869
I can count on her.

402
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:45,091
[bright cheery music]
[beastmen chattering]

403
00:16:45,221 --> 00:16:47,136
It turned out that the beast men
from Howling Village

404
00:16:47,267 --> 00:16:48,616
weren't trying to trick us.

405
00:16:48,746 --> 00:16:50,531
They really did want
trade relations.

406
00:16:50,661 --> 00:16:53,099
- Now then let's talk about
our trade agreement.

407
00:16:53,229 --> 00:16:54,361
- Yes.

408
00:16:54,491 --> 00:16:55,710
- Our trade's different.

409
00:16:55,840 --> 00:16:58,147
We trade physical goods
in an open market.

410
00:16:58,278 --> 00:17:01,237
After all, we don't use any
currency in our village.

411
00:17:01,368 --> 00:17:03,109
- That's the same as here.

412
00:17:03,239 --> 00:17:04,936
Currency, huh?

413
00:17:05,067 --> 00:17:07,765
I'm sure we'll need to
create it someday.

414
00:17:07,896 --> 00:17:11,291
- Normally I'd want to open up
a market in both villages

415
00:17:11,421 --> 00:17:15,425
but, if you can, we'd like you
to come to ours to trade.

416
00:17:15,556 --> 00:17:17,471
The truth is it was very
difficult for us

417
00:17:17,601 --> 00:17:19,038
to even get here
with our goods.

418
00:17:19,168 --> 00:17:20,604
- Oh?

419
00:17:20,735 --> 00:17:22,519
- Carrying them here and
back would be too much.

420
00:17:22,650 --> 00:17:24,913
- It would be pretty much the
same for us to travel as well.

421
00:17:25,044 --> 00:17:26,436
- But you live here.

422
00:17:26,567 --> 00:17:29,831
Aren't you able to navigate
the forest easily?

423
00:17:29,961 --> 00:17:31,615
- [Hiraku] Now that
he mentions it,

424
00:17:31,746 --> 00:17:36,272
maybe I can have Kuro and the
dogs carry the goods for us.

425
00:17:36,403 --> 00:17:37,839
I understand.
- Huh?

426
00:17:37,969 --> 00:17:40,189
- What would you like
for our first trade?

427
00:17:40,320 --> 00:17:41,625
- Well, we have
lots of goods

428
00:17:41,756 --> 00:17:43,279
made from the ore
that we mine.

429
00:17:43,410 --> 00:17:46,326
We have things like paints,
silverware, glassworks,

430
00:17:46,456 --> 00:17:47,849
and also metal works.

431
00:17:47,979 --> 00:17:50,678
- I want them, I wanna
have all of that stuff!

432
00:17:50,808 --> 00:17:53,463
- In exchange we'd like to get
some of the food you grow.

433
00:17:53,594 --> 00:17:54,986
- Then we'll bring
our food crops to trade

434
00:17:55,117 --> 00:17:55,944
at the open market.

435
00:17:56,075 --> 00:17:57,424
- Ah.

436
00:17:57,554 --> 00:17:59,991
- [Hiraku] And so began
our trade relationship

437
00:18:00,122 --> 00:18:02,255
with Howling Village.

438
00:18:03,647 --> 00:18:05,649
[leaves rustling]

439
00:18:07,521 --> 00:18:10,132
- About the present thing.
- Hmm?

440
00:18:10,263 --> 00:18:12,526
- The truth is,
until now I didn't know

441
00:18:12,656 --> 00:18:14,876
people brought gifts
when visiting.

442
00:18:15,006 --> 00:18:17,531
Our village doesn't have
a custom like that.

443
00:18:17,661 --> 00:18:20,360
- Oh, that's okay,
don't worry about it.

444
00:18:20,490 --> 00:18:22,405
- I'll bring
something next time.

445
00:18:22,536 --> 00:18:25,147
With that being said,
our village is poor,

446
00:18:25,278 --> 00:18:28,585
so we won't be able to
bring anything fancy.

447
00:18:28,716 --> 00:18:30,109
- Right, that's fine.

448
00:18:30,239 --> 00:18:31,936
What's important isn't
the value of the gift

449
00:18:32,067 --> 00:18:33,721
but the thought behind it.

450
00:18:33,851 --> 00:18:38,247
- Ah, hearing that from you
makes me feel better.

451
00:18:38,378 --> 00:18:40,858
[bright music]

452
00:18:44,297 --> 00:18:47,038
- I was planning on going
to the market as well.

453
00:18:47,169 --> 00:18:48,953
- You can't,
it looks bad if we send

454
00:18:49,084 --> 00:18:50,694
our top man there right away.

455
00:18:50,825 --> 00:18:51,913
- Is that how it works?

456
00:18:52,043 --> 00:18:53,349
- That's how it works.

457
00:18:53,480 --> 00:18:55,177
We drew lots and based on that,

458
00:18:55,308 --> 00:18:58,311
I'll be acting on your behalf
for the duration while there.

459
00:18:58,441 --> 00:19:01,357
- [Hiraku] Originally it was
going to take 10 days

460
00:19:01,488 --> 00:19:02,880
for them to travel,

461
00:19:03,011 --> 00:19:04,752
but Dryme agreed
to take everyone there

462
00:19:04,882 --> 00:19:08,234
in exchange for
a barrel of wine.

463
00:19:08,364 --> 00:19:10,018
After his first visit,

464
00:19:10,149 --> 00:19:12,934
Dryme started to come here
to hang out regularly.

465
00:19:13,064 --> 00:19:16,677
[Dryme groans]

466
00:19:16,807 --> 00:19:20,202
He always brings us gifts of
treasures or weapons with him

467
00:19:20,333 --> 00:19:22,335
so no one complains.

468
00:19:22,465 --> 00:19:24,989
Transporting everyone in
exchange for a barrel of wine

469
00:19:25,120 --> 00:19:26,991
was actually Dryme's idea.

470
00:19:27,122 --> 00:19:28,993
So I took him up on the offer.

471
00:19:29,124 --> 00:19:31,170
- Okay then, we'll off now.

472
00:19:31,300 --> 00:19:33,607
- Thanks for the wine, mayor.

473
00:19:33,737 --> 00:19:36,349
- Sure.
[wings crashing]

474
00:19:40,309 --> 00:19:41,876
[birds chirping]

475
00:19:42,006 --> 00:19:43,965
- Are they really
going to show up?

476
00:19:44,095 --> 00:19:47,055
Well, Garf worked out the
trade agreement with them.

477
00:19:47,186 --> 00:19:48,839
They'll be here.

478
00:19:48,970 --> 00:19:50,232
- We haven't even received word

479
00:19:50,363 --> 00:19:52,103
that they've reached
the mountain range yet.

480
00:19:52,234 --> 00:19:53,366
[wings flapping]
- Huh?

481
00:19:53,496 --> 00:19:55,150
Is that?

482
00:19:56,325 --> 00:19:57,587
- [Beastman] A dragon!

483
00:19:57,718 --> 00:20:00,242
- Yeah, and it's coming
straight this way.

484
00:20:01,330 --> 00:20:03,071
Look at that.

485
00:20:03,724 --> 00:20:05,639
[upbeat music]

486
00:20:05,769 --> 00:20:07,249
Good work, everyone.

487
00:20:07,380 --> 00:20:08,729
How was it?

488
00:20:08,859 --> 00:20:10,992
- We were able to exchange
everything we took

489
00:20:11,122 --> 00:20:12,559
and they loved it all.

490
00:20:12,689 --> 00:20:14,387
They seemed to be
hesitant at first

491
00:20:14,517 --> 00:20:17,041
because they wouldn't go
near anything we brought,

492
00:20:17,172 --> 00:20:20,610
but then I tried the free sample
stuff you told me about

493
00:20:20,741 --> 00:20:26,137
and before I knew it, a crowd
of beast people had gathered.

494
00:20:26,268 --> 00:20:28,705
- They sold the wine that was
supposed to be for me.

495
00:20:28,836 --> 00:20:30,054
- Did they?

496
00:20:30,185 --> 00:20:31,360
I guess you'll
just have to drink

497
00:20:31,491 --> 00:20:33,101
even more at dinner tonight.

498
00:20:33,232 --> 00:20:34,320
- You're the best.

499
00:20:34,450 --> 00:20:36,322
You really know
how to cheer me up.

500
00:20:36,452 --> 00:20:37,714
- In addition to that,

501
00:20:37,845 --> 00:20:39,542
the mayor of Howling Village
wanted to know

502
00:20:39,673 --> 00:20:42,110
if some of their people
could come and live here.

503
00:20:42,241 --> 00:20:45,069
- [grunts] We need
more people to work,

504
00:20:45,200 --> 00:20:46,854
so I'd be glad to have them.

505
00:20:46,984 --> 00:20:49,726
- There are 20 people that
want to come live here

506
00:20:49,857 --> 00:20:54,035
and they're all young women.

507
00:20:54,165 --> 00:20:56,037
- The fact of the matter is
that right now

508
00:20:56,167 --> 00:20:59,040
this village is in desperate
need of more men.

509
00:20:59,170 --> 00:21:02,086
If this keeps up, I'm afraid
the village won't have a future.

510
00:21:02,217 --> 00:21:05,307
Fine, but I have one condition.

511
00:21:05,438 --> 00:21:07,135
If they can send
at least two young men,

512
00:21:07,266 --> 00:21:09,833
then I'll happily
accept everyone.

513
00:21:09,964 --> 00:21:11,748
- Understood, mayor.
[upbeat music]

514
00:21:11,879 --> 00:21:14,751
- [Hiraku] Now the future of
the village is secure.

515
00:21:14,882 --> 00:21:16,753
[Sena whimpering]

516
00:21:16,884 --> 00:21:19,060
- Hello, my name is Sena.

517
00:21:19,190 --> 00:21:21,584
We are all very grateful
that you have accepted us

518
00:21:21,715 --> 00:21:23,499
into your village.

519
00:21:23,630 --> 00:21:26,981
We're mentally prepared for you
to use us however you see fit,

520
00:21:27,111 --> 00:21:29,853
just please don't
abandon us later on.

521
00:21:29,984 --> 00:21:32,943
- Uh, I see you've gone
through a lot to prepare

522
00:21:33,074 --> 00:21:34,380
for your move here.

523
00:21:34,510 --> 00:21:36,599
Anyways, we've got
your beds ready.

524
00:21:36,730 --> 00:21:39,123
Take your time and
get acclimated.

525
00:21:39,254 --> 00:21:40,864
- You want us to take our time?

526
00:21:40,995 --> 00:21:42,126
- Yes, please.

527
00:21:42,257 --> 00:21:43,911
Once you're used to
daily life here,

528
00:21:44,041 --> 00:21:46,130
you can make requests for
what kind of house you want.

529
00:21:46,261 --> 00:21:47,871
You don't need to
worry about us

530
00:21:48,002 --> 00:21:49,830
kicking you out
or anything.

531
00:21:51,266 --> 00:21:53,094
- Thank you so much, mayor.

532
00:21:53,224 --> 00:21:54,574
- Of course.

533
00:21:54,704 --> 00:21:56,793
By the way, are
the men here with you?

534
00:21:56,924 --> 00:21:58,317
- They are.

535
00:21:58,447 --> 00:22:00,144
We have brought three
of them along with us.

536
00:22:00,275 --> 00:22:02,103
[bright music]

537
00:22:02,233 --> 00:22:04,627
[children gasping]

538
00:22:04,758 --> 00:22:07,195
We brought you some young men
like you asked of us.

539
00:22:07,326 --> 00:22:08,849
- [Hiraku] Okay.

540
00:22:08,979 --> 00:22:12,461
No, wait, maybe five years,
or maybe 10 years from now.

541
00:22:12,592 --> 00:22:16,987
I'm counting on you for
the future of this village!

542
00:22:18,380 --> 00:22:21,688
["Feel the winds"
by Yui Hizuki plays]

543
00:23:47,643 --> 00:23:50,429
[rustic music playing]

